+\begin{enumerate}[leftmargin=1.6em]
+  \item \textbf{Visible-context commitment.} The map $\chi$ is defined before running the ablations and is used identically by all non-oracle policies. In \textsc{Berth-1-Conflict}, $\chi$ may include vessel class, queue state, weather regime, disruption family, operating mode, time bucket, berth slot, and ETA bin, but not latent readiness, crane safety, weather admissibility, or claim provenance.
+  \item \textbf{Dominance commitment.} The dominance scheme $\mathcal D$ is registered by proposition family. It cannot be tuned after seeing paired deltas.
+  \item \textbf{Solver-isolation commitment.} The policy code, action costs, episode bank, and random seeds are fixed across all ablations. Conditions change only the claim-state semantics.
+  \item \textbf{Evidence-status commitment.} Synthetic smoke tests are pipeline checks, not evidence. Paper evidence begins only when the same frozen interface is run on a replay bank or a declared synthetic benchmark with locked parameters.
+\end{enumerate}
